Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> program
Rule 1     program -> sentence SEMICOLON program
Rule 2     program -> <empty>
Rule 3     sentence -> expresion SEMICOLON
Rule 4     expresion -> expresion PLUS expresion
Rule 5     expresion -> expresion MINUS expresion
Rule 6     expresion -> expresion TIMES expresion
Rule 7     expresion -> expresion DIVIDE expresion
Rule 8     expresion -> MINUS expresion
Rule 9     expresion -> L_PAREN expresion R_PAREN
Rule 10    expresion -> NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

DIVIDE               : 7
L_PAREN              : 9
MINUS                : 5 8
NUMBER               : 10
PLUS                 : 4
R_PAREN              : 9
SEMICOLON            : 1 3
TIMES                : 6
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

expresion            : 3 4 4 5 5 6 6 7 7 8 9
program              : 1 0
sentence             : 1

Parsing method: LALR

